# fonts-noto-extra: the fonts for every script the browser meets that
# fonts-jamos does not cover (the FONTS track, docs/G2-PLAN.md "GP2 notes,
# continued"), a data port like fonts-jamos (style data: files and no build).
# The owner asked for full coverage, so a page in any language shows text and
# not boxes.
#
# What is in it, all Noto Sans, all SIL OFL 1.1, the static unhinted TrueType
# files (FreeType's own hinting does the rest):
#   CJK        Noto Sans CJK 2.004's two OpenType collections, Regular and Bold,
#              from googlefonts/noto-cjk at its Sans2.004 tag (a collection is
#              one file of 19 or 20 MB: the JP, KR, SC, TC and HK faces, and the
#              Mono ones, over one set of outlines); fonts.conf picks the face by
#              the page's language
#   scripts    Arabic, Hebrew, Devanagari, Bengali, Tamil, Telugu, Gujarati,
#              Gurmukhi (Punjabi), Kannada, Malayalam, Thai, Georgian,
#              Armenian, Ethiopic, and Khmer, Lao, Myanmar, Sinhala, Oriya
#              (Odia) beyond the owner's list, each Regular and Bold where
#              the release has both
#   symbols    Noto Sans Symbols (Regular, Bold), Symbols 2 and Math (Regular
#              only: they have no Bold)
# Not in it: Noto Serif for any script (the CJK and Indic text of a page asking
# for a serif falls to these sans faces), Thai Looped, Tamil Supplement,
# Tibetan (the release is a Serif), Syriac, Thaana, Mongolian and the historic
# scripts. Noto Sans, Serif, Sans Mono and Noto Color Emoji (Latin, Greek,
# Cyrillic, Vietnamese and emoji) are fonts-jamos's.
#
# Where the script fonts come from: the notofonts GitHub organisation builds each
# script from its own repository and puts the fonts in that repository's release
# zip (NotoSansArabic-v2.013.zip, 5 to 35 MB, every width and weight hinted and
# not, static and variable) and in notofonts.github.io, its website's
# repository. The zips' files and the website's at the commit below are the same
# bytes (checked file by file for every font here), and the website's are one
# small file each at one pin; five of the zips (Ethiopic, Gurmukhi, Malayalam,
# Myanmar, Tamil) also carry members named ../AUTHORS.txt, which the builder
# refuses to unpack. So each font is a source of its own at that commit, with
# the size and SHA-256 of the file. The releases they are: Arabic 2.013, Hebrew
# 3.001, Devanagari 2.007, Bengali 3.011, Tamil 2.004, Telugu 2.005, Gujarati
# 2.106, Gurmukhi 2.004, Kannada 2.006, Malayalam 2.104, Thai 2.002, Georgian
# 2.005, Armenian 2.008, Ethiopic 2.102, Khmer 2.004, Lao 2.003, Myanmar 2.107,
# Sinhala 3.000, Oriya 2.007, Symbols 2.003, Symbols 2 2.008, Math 3.000.
#
# Each licence text is a file of its own in the package
# (share/licences/fonts-noto-extra/), taken from the project's repository at the
# tag of the release (the notofonts repositories' OFL.txt each carry their own
# copyright line, so each project has its own file; Symbols and Symbols 2 are
# one repository and share one).
#
# The fontconfig side: share/fonts/noto-extra/fonts.conf names this package's
# directory, the families' places in the generic lists (after fonts-jamos's)
# and the CJK face for each language. fonts-jamos's fonts.conf includes it
# when it is installed (and fonts-jamos is what the browser's /etc/fonts/fonts.conf
# includes), so this package `runs` fonts-jamos.
name        fonts-noto-extra
version     1.0
revision    1
summary     the Noto fonts for CJK, Arabic, Hebrew, the Indic and Southeast Asian scripts, Georgian, Armenian, Ethiopic and symbols
homepage    https://github.com/notofonts/notofonts.github.io
category    data
licence     OFL-1.1
licence-file noto-cjk-OFL.txt noto-arabic-OFL.txt noto-hebrew-OFL.txt noto-devanagari-OFL.txt noto-bengali-OFL.txt noto-tamil-OFL.txt noto-telugu-OFL.txt noto-gujarati-OFL.txt noto-gurmukhi-OFL.txt noto-kannada-OFL.txt noto-malayalam-OFL.txt noto-thai-OFL.txt noto-georgian-OFL.txt noto-armenian-OFL.txt noto-ethiopic-OFL.txt noto-khmer-OFL.txt noto-lao-OFL.txt noto-myanmar-OFL.txt noto-sinhala-OFL.txt noto-oriya-OFL.txt noto-symbols-OFL.txt noto-math-OFL.txt
